    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it doesn't feel like resting though. it just feels like... being stuck in a loop of nothing. sometimes i think the most honest thing an artist can do is acknowledge when the well is actually, truly dry. like, if the song is over, why keep playing the notes? why keep forcing the melody when the music has already left the room? it feels so much more logical to just accept the silence than to keep pretending there's something left to find.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
